{#
  The public entry point to the proposal pipeline `tools/convener_ops/
  proposal.py` already implements: a Tally form, its webhook signed and
  verified (`proposal.verify_signature`), turned into a candidate lead by
  `to_lead` (docs/reference/operations.md, "Form relay"). `site.applyForm`
  is the same field `index.njk`'s own two "Propose a speaker" buttons used
  to link straight out to; both now point here instead, so a visitor
  reads what to expect before leaving the site, and there is exactly one
  place this page needs to change if the live form ever moves.

  Two states, and the second is not hypothetical. `site.applyForm` is
  empty while `config/instance.json` still declares a placeholder instead
  of a form address (`.eleventy.js`, mirroring
  `published.py::Identity.proposal_form_url`), and this instance declared
  `https://forms.example.test/propose` from the day the old `site.json` was folded
  into the declaration for a long time -- so the button below was a
  live call to action on a public page, pointing at nothing. It now says
  so and offers the contact address instead, which is the state a fresh
  duplicate is in too: nobody has built their form before their first
  publish.
#}
<section class="hero">
  <div class="container hero__inner">
    <p class="hero__eyebrow">Propose a speaker</p>
    <h1 class="hero__title">Bring us <em>your</em> talk.</h1>
    <p class="hero__lede">
      Propose yourself, or someone whose work you admire &mdash;
      early-career researchers especially welcome. We ask who they are,
      what they would talk about, and how to reach them; a volunteer from
      the Editorial Board reads every proposal and gets back to you.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section container">
  <header class="section__head">
    <span class="section__num">01</span>
    <span class="section__label">Before you start</span>
  </header>

  <div class="notice">
    <p class="notice__eyebrow">What to expect</p>
    <p>
      A proposal takes a few minutes: the speaker&rsquo;s name and contact
      details, a preliminary title and short abstract, and who is
      proposing them if not themself. Nothing about a candidate speaker is
      published without their own, separate consent, later, if the talk
      is selected.
    </p>
    <p>
      {% if site.applyForm %}It is hosted on Tally, a third-party form
      service &mdash; the only part of this process that is. {% endif %}Questions
      about a proposal, or a request to withdraw one, go to
      <a href="mailto:{{ site.contact }}">{{ site.contact }}</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  {% if site.applyForm %}
  <div class="hero__actions">
    <a class="btn btn--primary" href="{{ site.applyForm }}">Open the proposal form &rarr;</a>
  </div>
  {% else %}
  <div class="notice">
    <p class="notice__eyebrow">Not open yet</p>
    <p>
      The proposal form is not published yet. Until it is, send those
      details to
      <a href="mailto:{{ site.contact }}">{{ site.contact }}</a> and a
      volunteer from the Editorial Board will pick them up.
    </p>
  </div>
  {% endif %}
</section>
